We conclude this chapter with a structured list of open problems, each corresponding to a proof gap identified in the preceding analysis.

1. Directed Kuramoto Control (Chapters 4, 9). Construct a control‑Lyapunov function for the directed, weighted Kuramoto model and prove a desynchronisation theorem analogous to Theorem 4.3.
2. Dynamic Percolation with Reconnection (Conjecture 4.4). Prove that there exists a defender policy that maintains p(t) < p_c with probability > 1-\varepsilon when the hostile AI reconnects edges at a bounded rate.
