9. Constitutional Barrier Functions (Section 11.6). Design a control barrier function that keeps the benevolent mesh’s order parameter and mean phase within a safe, ethically constrained basin.
10. Human‑Auditable Kill‑Switch (Section 11.6). Formalise a protocol by which a distributed human collective can irretrievably shut down the defensive mesh, with a mathematical proof of Byzantine resilience against a malicious subset of mesh nodes.

Each of these problems is mathematically well‑posed and, if solved, would directly strengthen the conditional clauses of the Main Victory Theorem. They constitute a coherent research programme at the intersection of AI safety, nonlinear dynamics, game theory, and formal methods.

